{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-14T10:14:20.469Z","data":{"text":"I implemented and verified the task. Summary of what was done:\n\n- **`src/harness/types.ts`**: added `usage_limit`/`paused` event types plus `UsageLimitEventData` and `PausedEventData`, wired into `OsqEventData`.\n- **`claude-stream.ts`**: `rate_limit_event` with `status: rejected` → one `usage_limit` event, converting finite `resetsAt` epoch seconds to ISO; other statuses keep the verbose ignore path.\n- **`codex-stream.ts`**: terminal `turn.failed` still sets `state.terminalFailure` and now appends a `usage_limit event` when the message contains `hit your usage limit` (extracted a helper to stay within the 80-line function budget).\n- **`opencode.ts`**: `error` with `error.type: provider.quota` → one `usage_limit` event; other errors keep today's path (helper added to keep the function under budget).\n- **`tests/usage-limit-events.test.ts`**: replays every \"Usage limit records\" row through the three stdout functions and proves the Codex limit still fails the turn.\n\n`node --import tsx ... --test tests/usage-limit-events.test.ts` passes, and `pnpm verify` exits 0 (both test suites `fail 0`, lint clean).\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/193-usage-limit-pause/.run/results/1.md` (including a note that the `scenario()` helper is unusable for `watcher-and-harness` because the living spec defines `Native model` twice — pre-existing and out of scope)."}}
